    "takeaway": "Colonial withdrawal produced new states, but those states were defined by boundaries drawn by someone else. Where those boundaries cut through communities, the result was conflict and mass displacement (Partition, Nakba). Where new states gained control of their economies, they typically chose state direction over free markets. And where migration corridors had been built under empire, they continued, keeping former colonies economically tied to former metropoles even after independence.",
