    "takeaway": "KC-6.2.IV.E identifies three causes of the Cold War's end: (1) U.S. military and technological development, specifically SDI and the shift to microelectronics-based military competition, created pressure the Soviet economy was structurally unable to match; (2) the Soviet invasion of Afghanistan became a nine-year failure that drained resources, disillusioned the public, and signaled Soviet limits to Eastern Europe; (3) public discontent and economic weakness in communist countries, exposed and amplified by Gorbachev's glasnost and perestroika, produced the 1989 Eastern European revolutions and the 1991 Soviet dissolution. The AP skill is explaining how these three causes interacted and compounded each other, not just listing them.",
